[C] exact SU(2) character coefficients and the identity  SUM (n+1)c_n = e^beta
================================================================================
  modified-Bessel source: scipy.special.iv
  beta= 0.02083:  SUM(n+1)c_n = 1.0210518621   e^beta = 1.0210518621   rel.err=0.00e+00
  beta= 1.00000:  SUM(n+1)c_n = 2.7182818285   e^beta = 2.7182818285   rel.err=1.63e-16
  beta= 2.50000:  SUM(n+1)c_n = 12.1824939607   e^beta = 12.1824939607   rel.err=8.75e-16
  => c_n = I_n - I_{n+2} is exact; u(beta)=c_1/c_0 is the single-plaquette activity.

  CALIBRATION-FREE diluteness diagnostic:  trivial-weight fraction f0 = c_0/e^beta
  (a convergent character/polymer expansion needs the nontrivial plaquettes DILUTE, f0 -> 1)
    beta= 0.02083:  c_0=1.000054  f0=c_0/e^beta=0.97944  (Phi(0)=(e^beta-c_0)/c_0=0.0210 nontrivial/trivial)
    beta= 1.00000:  c_0=1.130318  f0=c_0/e^beta=0.41582  (Phi(0)=(e^beta-c_0)/c_0=1.4049 nontrivial/trivial)
    beta= 2.50000:  c_0=2.013373  f0=c_0/e^beta=0.16527  (Phi(0)=(e^beta-c_0)/c_0=5.0508 nontrivial/trivial)
  f0: 0.98 (wall, dilute) -> 0.42 (beta=1) -> 0.165 (beta=2.5, DENSE);  expansion dead.

