================================================================================
[E] KP / Ursell ratio  rho_Ur(beta)=lambda_a Phi(1,beta)  at the P3 wall, beta=1, beta=2.5
================================================================================
  convergence of the connected-polymer (Ursell) series  <=>  rho_Ur < 1
  lambda_a = e*Delta (crude P3 animal constant);  Delta=20/12/4 for d=4/3/2
       beta          u         Phi(1) |      d=4 rho      d=3 rho      d=2 rho
    0.02083   0.010416   5.784773e-02 |   3.1449e+00   1.8870e+00   6.2899e-01
    0.10000   0.049979   3.011526e-01 |   1.6372e+01   9.8234e+00   3.2745e+00
    1.00000   0.480387   7.715963e+00 |   4.1948e+02   2.5169e+02   8.3897e+01
    2.50000   1.014390   8.518215e+01 |   4.6310e+03   2.7786e+03   9.2620e+02
  (all three exceed 1 already by beta~O(1); at 2.5 they are astronomically >1.)

  crude KP threshold (d=4):  convergence needs u < 1/lambda_a = 0.01839
  actual u(2.5) = 1.01439   => factor 55.1x too large
  rho_Ur(2.5)/rho_Ur(1/48) = 1472.5x  (d=4): 3.14 at the wall -> 4.631e+03 at 2.5
  crude rho_Ur=1 (d=4) is crossed at beta* ~ 0.00673; 2.5 is 372x beyond it
  u(beta)=1/lambda_a is reached only at beta ~ 0.03679  (u~beta/2 small-beta)
  (SZZ/BE wall is beta<1/48~0.02083; the crude KP constant is even tighter --
   either way beta=2.5 is 10^1-10^3 x beyond the wall.)

