[H] acid test: free field beta->inf -- activity does NOT decay; f1^2(free)=0 by structure
================================================================================
  beta     u=c1/c0      Phi(1)        rho_Ur(d=4)
    5.00   1.438681     1.4307e+03     7.7782e+04
   10.00   1.708371     1.0636e+05     5.7821e+06
   50.00   1.940306     1.4394e+16     7.8253e+17
  u -> 2 (c1/c0 -> 2) as beta->inf; activities grow, rho_Ur -> inf.
  The diagnostic correctly says 'no expansion' on the free field, and the free
  composite trF^2 has f1^2=0 (2-gluon cut) -- so the no-go never claims a false atom.

